Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook — Stephen Lower (@gc-chem1: 0, is #reference, #part-of @gc-sources) { r_0NFQA43WZVMECZY6SKZJMRXWBZ
Stephen Lower, retired faculty, Simon Fraser University. Chem1 General Chemistry Virtual Textbook. [Author's complete textbook and unit menu](https://chem1.com/acad/webtext/virtualtextbook.html). English.

Read the full introductory and first/second-semester units, then the relevant advanced units. Its connected lessons offer a second substantial explanation of the same foundations. Use the named topic when its unit numbering differs from another textbook. Advanced acid/base calculation, Q versus K, thermodynamics, redox, electrochemistry, kinetics, and the measurement units are especially useful for examining a simplistic first explanation.

The author states CC BY 3.0 Unported for the virtual textbook. Preserve author, source, actual edition/date, and separately credited components when reusing. This trail writes original connecting explanations and links assigned readings rather than mirroring the collection. Author, structure, licence, and availability checked on 29 October 2026.

